  "format": "40-card",
  "strategy": "enlist trample-funnel aggro",
  "colors": "RG",
  "identity": "Red-green enlist beatdown that treats enlist as a power-funnel rather than a keyword. Enlist is zero-sum by default - it taps a creature that could have attacked - so this build only ever funnels into a body blockers cannot absorb: Coalition Warbrute's trample, Linebreaker Baloth's 'can't be blocked by creatures with power 2 or less', or a kicked Colossal Growth granting trample on demand. Only two card names in the entire RG pool carry Enlist together with evasion, which is the ceiling this archetype has in this cube; Colossal Growth is the third payoff name because it MANUFACTURES the sink on a body already attacking. Cheap 3-power bodies (Yavimaya Iconoclast, Hexbane Tortoise) attack on turns 2-4 and are then spent as fuel on the alpha turn, with Hammerhand removing the one blocker that would otherwise eat it.",
